Sigrid Haugset will go into Tuesday's fourth stage individual time trial at the Women's Tour de France sporting the race leader's yellow jersey, after a dazzling ride to claim Monday's third stage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cdf7b85a-8fdb-11f1-b5e9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/sigrid-hausget.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cdf7b85a-8fdb-11f1-b5e9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/sigrid-hausget.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">384c2c1a-8fda-11f1-8ed9-75c61b62a88b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 11:19:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cdf7b85a-8fdb-11f1-b5e9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/sigrid-hausget.jpg">REUTERS - Denis Balibouse</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Cameroon edge past Ghana to reach last eight at Women's Africa Cup of Nations</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260802-cameroon-edge-past-ghana-to-reach-last-eight-at-2026-wafcon</link><description>
Cameroon beat Ghana 1-0 on Sunday night in Casablanca to move into the quarter-finals at the 2026 Women's Africa Cup of Nations, while Mali relaunched their campaign with a 3-2 victory over tournament debutantes Cape Verde.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7f7564ec-8ec9-11f1-acb5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/stuffy.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7f7564ec-8ec9-11f1-acb5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/stuffy.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d75dff72-8e6d-11f1-9fa6-a7feb290f265</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 23:31:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7f7564ec-8ec9-11f1-acb5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/stuffy.jpg">BackpagePix - Nabil Ramdani/BackpagePix</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Wiebes triumphs again to set stage win record at Women's Tour de France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260802-wiebes-triumphs-again-to-set-stage-win-record-at-women-s-tour-de-france</link><description>
Lorena Wiebes from the Netherlands won her second consecutive stage at the 2026 Women's Tour de France on Sunday to set a record of seven stage victories in the five-year-old race.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d0c617e8-8ebe-11f1-98ef-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/wibese.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d0c617e8-8ebe-11f1-98ef-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/wibese.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c31592a-8ea7-11f1-9a16-27f4398d8a9e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:15:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d0c617e8-8ebe-11f1-98ef-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/wibese.jpg">Jean-Christophe Bott/Keystone vi - Jean-Christophe Bott</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Björkegren expects 'better Ghana' against Cameroon at 2026 WAFCON</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260802-bj%C3%B6rkegren-expects-better-ghana-against-cameroon-at-2026-wafcon</link><description>
Ghana head coach Kim Björkegren predicted a better performance from his side in their group stage game against Cameroon on Sunday night at the 2026 women's Africa Cup of Nations (WAFCON).
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e0335ce-8e67-11f1-be08-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/kim-Bjo%CC%88rkegren-gfa.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e0335ce-8e67-11f1-be08-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/kim-Bjo%CC%88rkegren-gfa.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43adc922-8e56-11f1-9be4-81e7f72f4ffb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:06:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7e0335ce-8e67-11f1-be08-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/kim-Bjo%CC%88rkegren-gfa.jpg">© Ghana Football Association</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Wiebes claims opening stage of Women’s Tour de France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260801-wiebes-claims-opening-stage-of-women-s-tour-de-france</link><description>
Lorena Wiebes won the opening stage of the 2026 Women’s Tour de France on Saturday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/82abea16-8df0-11f1-a29b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/wiebes-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/82abea16-8df0-11f1-a29b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/wiebes-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fbbb5aec-8dee-11f1-bef9-dd360c7dec1f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 21:33:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/82abea16-8df0-11f1-a29b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/wiebes-1.jpg">Jean-Christophe Bott/Keystone vi - Jean-Christophe Bott</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>European football chiefs say they have lost confidence in Fifa boss Infantino</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260801-european-football-chiefs-say-they-have-lost-confidence-in-fifa-boss-infantino</link><description>
European football's governing body Uefa on Saturday said it had lost confidence in the Fifa boss Gianni Infantino after world football's ruling organisation abandoned plans to sell a stake in the commercial rights to the World Cup.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a783c36a-8d8a-11f1-a6e3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26213254624609.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a783c36a-8d8a-11f1-a6e3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26213254624609.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">79713c88-8da7-11f1-98f6-7947e37c67d0</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 14:59:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a783c36a-8d8a-11f1-a6e3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26213254624609.jpg">DARRYL DYCK/The Canadian Press v - DARRYL DYCK</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>No go for Infantino: how Fifa's World Cup private investment plan imploded</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260801-no-go-for-infantino-how-fifa-s-world-cup-private-investment-plan-imploded</link><description>
The world's most powerful football administrator Gianni Infantino on Saturday yielded to the international collective when he pulled the plug on a plan to allow private investment in the World Cup. His proposals for world football's governing body Fifa to reform its commercial operations had sparked a furious backlash.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f31c9020-8445-11f1-8a7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T000943Z-1234957518-UP1EM7J1UL3TE-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f31c9020-8445-11f1-8a7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T000943Z-1234957518-UP1EM7J1UL3TE-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">53e5b36e-8d97-11f1-9812-fffbeee1baf8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 11:41:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f31c9020-8445-11f1-8a7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T000943Z-1234957518-UP1EM7J1UL3TE-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-WORLDCUP-ESP-ARG.jpg">REUTERS - Lee Smith</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Fifa boss Infantino scraps plan to sell off World Cup profits to private equity</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260801-fifa-boss-infantino-scraps-plan-to-sell-off-world-cup-profits-to-private-equity-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Gianni Infantino, the boss of world football's governing body Fifa, caved to international pressure on Saturday and abandoned his plan to sell World Cup profits to private equity.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6187729e-8d3a-11f1-919e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-28T162945Z-1037867588-RC28KJAED3SY-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-FIFA-STAKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6187729e-8d3a-11f1-919e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-28T162945Z-1037867588-RC28KJAED3SY-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-FIFA-STAKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a71431d2-8d7e-11f1-91b7-f716cf42b3e4</guid><pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 09:34:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6187729e-8d3a-11f1-919e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-28T162945Z-1037867588-RC28KJAED3SY-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-FIFA-STAKE.jpg">© Benoit Tessier / REUTERS</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Women's Tour de France pits France's Ferrand-Prévot against history</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260801-women-s-tour-de-france-pits-france-s-ferrand-pr%C3%A9vot-against-history</link><description>
France's star cyclist Pauline Ferrand-Prévot will set off on Saturday as one of the favourites for the 2026 Women's Tour de France. The 34-year-old will also be seeking a slice of cycling history. No rider has retained the crown since the competition started in 2022.
